50:* ''Branch'': `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5`. `git rev-list --count origin/feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5..HEAD` reads the unpushed commits. The controlling session pushes, only a head whose shard run read green and only while no CI run stands in flight (`git push origin <sha>:refs/heads/feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5`); no lane pushes. Green has two halves: the shard run, and the branch's full CI, which `node tools/ci-verdict.mjs --head <sha>` reads as green, red or unread (a detached worktree names `--branch feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5`; the tool refuses a detached head without one). The same command prints a third reading beside them, the held-out container drivers: the run that names the head, or else the newest run the branch holds, with that run's head, the commits between and each driver's result. A head no held-out run measured reads unread there, never green; the third reading says and never moves the exit code. Never a lane's to move, commit, stash or revert: `.worktrees/`, `.claude/worktrees/`, the `mempalace` submodule pointer, and the `VSCode-TW5-Syntax` pointer, which the operator pins at the released grammar while the grammar's own head stands ahead of that pin.
53:* ''Witness fleet'': `bash tools/witness-all.sh`, the whole fleet, one run at a time, by the controlling session and never by a lane that works beside other hands; a hand-picked subset reads greener than the tree. It holds out the witnesses its own `HELD_OUT` table names (the docker, browser and tree-clean ones). Capture its exit code directly, never through a pipe; `git status --porcelain` reads identical before and after a sound run.
57:* ''Island doors'': `tools/capability-inventory-witness.sh` measures which vessel doors (fetch · rest · custody write · dyad) each island of the node and web assemblies reaches on the built tree, and every source call that spawns an island or attaches it a door, against the committed table `tools/capability-inventory.json`. The table measures reach, never a door's policy (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/harbor#/the-harnesses">>). A door a class reaches where the table says it did not, a new or extra seam, a seam that left or a new ask reads red by name; a deliberate change re-writes the table in the commit that makes it (`node tools/capability-inventory.mjs --write`). A browser wiki or session island reaches no door and meets the dyad refusal; the browser's daemon island reads `unmeasured`, since its spawn seam stands inside `openBrowserVessel`; a session island's view asks run through the pool core's own listener, which no row drives.
