98:* ''The live test runs with TWO operators on two machines from its first day'': the operator and the operator's daughter, in one house. The face-switch act, the cabal plane, the custody seal and the engine fold ALL land before it.
102:* ''Face plurality stands as a day-one requirement.'' Each of the two humans wears at least three faces, each with a public Handle, on the first Nexus.
105:* ''All CODE runs dockerized''; the host keeps only the hooks into the operator's environment (files and bags, session capture, the editor and CLI entry, custody).
106:* ''ONE Lararium per HUMAN, never per face.'' A human's faces keep their data together in one vessel (`PRIVATE-all, PUBLIC-one`); the recorded face-switch act carries plurality. No design assumes a container or a state mount per face.
107:* ''A SESSION wears the face; the vessel wears none'' (operator-ruled; quote license: //"a human might want a tab open as one Persona, and a tab open as another Persona... same vessel. Identity as relation."// and //"a CLI session wears its own face too … those act as ephemeral UX"//). A vessel holds its roots and one store. A session — a browser tab, a CLI run — contracts in as ONE persona, and several sessions may live at once over one vessel, each wearing its own. Every act carries exactly one face. Two faces live from one vessel never link on the wire: each session proves itself under its own face-scoped key, never under a key the vessel shares across them. The vessel-wide parts (custody, the daemon island) serve every session and let none read another's planes.
108:* ''Local-first first.'' Cloud "backup larariums" under other humans' delegated keys stand DEFERRED until the operator can deploy to a cloud surface. Nothing in the container or the face-switch work may foreclose a keyless ciphertext carrier later.
113:* ''Lapse rides a causal fence'': an epoch roll, a burn marker, or causal supersession at a verified relation fence. A replica missing that history reports an incomplete view, never "expired"; quiet never means lapse.
129:* ''Steward signing.'' A scoped face signs acts that belong to one person; a transparent quorum Handle signs acts the collective owns; the root never appears publicly. A human wears MANY faces and many public Handles, each in many cabals, and signs a steward edge with the face or Handle worn IN THAT CABAL.
