472:* `G34` A removal no reader can keep refuses by name (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/automerge-doc-store">>). The store lands a based removal a concurrent writer overrode, then surfaces it to a listening reader alone: with no parallel-drafts reader it drops the surfacing with no word, and a reader that throws earns one console line while the write stands (`automerge-doc-store.ts`, `parallel-drafts.ts`). Owed: the refusal by name before any change lands, wherever no reader stands or every reader failed, with the store authoring no draft of its own; and the durable conflict handle the refusal carries (the document, the removal's request id, the conflicting change and head identities, never the hand's text), at a home where a hand whose editor went offline finds it again. G.
473:* `G35` The disk watcher's standing instruction (#/rulings; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/api/disk-projection#/projection-law">>). Owed: the instruction as a record the operator signs by a human route, naming one bag, a path pattern and a per-wave count ceiling, which no automated seat signs; the watcher's settle of each pending removal it covers through the shore's removal door; the audit row that names the instruction a removal rode; `lares shore restore` over a settled removal; and a mass vanish past the ceiling, a standoff, or a removal outside the pattern left pending for a person (`packages/lares-cli/src/commands/watch.ts`, `shore-verb.ts`, `disk-projector.ts`). G.
481:* `K17` The edge frontier (#/rulings, the edge frontier, 2026-10-20). Red-first: the frontier certificate and its verifier on node and browser alike; the signed empty genesis at every founding; registration of a raise into its signer's next frontier; the widening reader (admit, grant, a content-key seal) acting as of a qualifying frontier and waiting as unknown otherwise; the admit bundle carrying the frontier and its snapshot; the reader persisting its highest accepted head. Reds: a withheld first raise, a deleted local raise, a stale clean frontier, two conflicting frontiers, a missing snapshot, a concurrent raise and lower, an epoch rollover. Beside Wave C, on the spine. K. The fleet board's frontier stands built with Wave C. The realm leg, K17-R (kit `docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane`, the operator's rulings on forks 3 and 4, 2026-10-22), landed in PR #97 on 2026-10-26: one lease law, so a Nexus or realm lease rises only on a charter quorum's signed advance read under its seal-epoch lineage and the unsigned max-register retires with no reader left; each voucher signs its own hand's frontier; a seal roll signs every anchored realm's head under the new epoch; a split-seat cosign carries its head; and the realm admit bundle carries the board's acts, frontiers and snapshots, so a joiner holding no board acts as of them. Owed to `K18`: a closed roster's keys can still raise the lease (stale more, never less) until the recovery door closes that window; the fold never lowers.
483:* `K16` The Teshima Family Council (#/rulings, 2026-10-18; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/cabal-realm">>), `K15`'s acceptance story. Kalani founds a private council; Leilani joins it with two of her three faces. Red-first, after `K15`'s face context: (1) the council's hive as a Keyhive group holding no key of its own, its members the chosen faces' own identities; (2) an invite walks Leilani to the door, the threshold grafts each chosen face, a face leaves by its own act, and another's removal rides `kapae` or a fork by omission; (3) a member face's photo lands in its working layer of the council wiki and reaches the council's canon by `MOVE` (`W27`); (4) both chosen faces read it, the face kept back reads nothing and learns nothing, and no event in the council's history names a creator or issuer that ties two of Leilani's faces together; (5) a herm carries the sealed book and authors nothing (`K15` step 5). The e2e set stands four vessels: Kalani's, one per chosen face of Leilani's, and a herm. The e2e set walks the council at one hearth first: Kalani's seed charter holds the realm and Leilani's chosen faces walk there as guests, no Nexus founded (#/rulings, one charter). The two-hearth council follows, under the Nexus the two found, and there the member consult that lets a realm's documents cross between two operators reads a root map nothing fills (cabal-realm #/many-realms, owed), and the climb from seed charter to Nexus re-pins the realm by a named act (owed). Open joints: a quorum Handle with a seated key stands only where the council signs as one name, and that key signs collective acts alone, reaching no member's hive (#/the-steward-signer, owed). K, W.
