# K15 bonds — no seed reaches past the floor: the Episkopos brief (controller, 2026-10-26)

Mask: **Bond-Wright: Lares (Tasked Spirit)**, the K15-bonds Episkopos, fresh lane, slot three (after G15 lands).

## Why this lane
Road :208 (operator, 2026-10-19): custody and identity read by capability, never by host. "A node's daemon auth,
device-key signer, sibling enrolment and group-secret opener read the one vessel seed today ... each is a bond owed,
carried by K15." W29's seed census names them as K15 exceptions. The operator ruled (2026-10-26) to close open work
before the X0 bake; these bonds move identity bytes, so they precede X0. Two ratcheted scout rounds mapped every bond:
`/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/k15-bonds/{sol,luna}/{out,out2}.md` (read all four first). No operator question
survived.

## Read first, in order
1. `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/noosphere-boot.mem`.
2. `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/controller-handoff.mem` #/the-lane-law and `docs/pono/mixed-model-swarm.mem`.
3. The road: :203 (one Keyhive identity per PersonaGroup), :206–:208, the `K15` row; kits `docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem`,
   `k15-wave-d-lane.mem`, `k15-custody-step-zero.mem`, `w29-place-kel-lane.mem` (#/owed); `tools/seed-census.mjs`.
4. The four scout handbacks above.

## The model you enact (settled)
- RETIRE the vessel-wide Keyhive Individual, its Archive and the place ContactCard as general peer proof. Each
  PersonaGroup keeps its own Keyhive identity keyed by its face atom (Waves C and D built that); place founding and face
  founding split, and the place mints no Keyhive identity at all.
- EVERY FACE OPERATION (dial, join, device edge, enrolment, sibling channel, daemon proof, group-secret open, internal face
  ask, `lares meme` promotion) signs or opens by the EXPLICITLY SELECTED face's atom under its FCK. Several faces need a
  named face; ambiguity and no face refuse by name (the command names its face; I1's CLI takes `--face N`). Internal asks
  sort per call by the relation they protect; no shared S key.
- A FACELESS VESSEL (a bare herm, a floor-only node) needs no Keyhive identity: the Automerge Repo peer id routes
  transport only and `shareConfig` reads policy, not identity (measured: `open-node-vessel.ts:863-930`,
  `island-repo.ts:94-108`). It carries public and ciphertext bytes and signs only the five floor duties under the scoped
  place signer (W29); it refuses face gates, Keyhive creation, daemon face auth, group-secret open and meme signature.
  `carriageIdentity`'s place arm retires; the carriage presents the public place card and pin.
- THE RELAY KEY: a random, durable, relay-only S row on the node, the relay service its principal and a relay-only opener
  (road :207: the house names an S row's principal and opener), rotated explicitly; no derivation from the place seed, no
  environment-seed fallback, no face or daemon authority. Its public pin re-pins the relay address.
- CADENCE: `nodeSeedHex` leaves `carriage-caps`; cadence jitter takes a public place id or fresh local randomness.
- OLD BYTES: no CRDT document survives until X0, so re-genesis replaces migration; an old mixed archive, a place-arm card
  and a vessel-key signature on a face relation refuse by name.
- THE CENSUS GOES TRANSITIVE: the token census sees spellings, not dataflow (the scouts list every renamed parameter:
  `foundThePlace`'s `vesselSeed`, `daemonAuth.seed` into `bootDaemonKeyhive`, `nodeSeedHex`, `signerSeed`, `gateSeed`,
  the `sign` callbacks, `vesselGateKey` and the verifying-key aliases). Add a handoff ledger or an alias-following check so
  a renamed parameter carrying the seed reads red; prove it on a planted renamed consumer (silent-zero). Burn each K15
  census exception only when its replacement and its positive land.

## The slices (one lane, in order; each red with its control and known positive)
1. Identity bytes: split place and face founding; retire the place Individual, ContactCard, mixed Archive and bare leaf
   (`ceremony-core`, `keyhive-provider`, `place-card`, node `commands/init`, `leaf-identity`, `browser-vessel-identity`,
   browser founding in `open-browser-vessel`). Red: the place-seed thief mints or restores no face identity. Control: the
   selected A atom restores A, B stays shut, a faceless public card reads.
2. Face runtime and wire proofs: `boot-daemon-keyhive`, `operator-daemon-behavior`, node and browser opens, sibling,
   enrolment, group-secret, `lares-cli` `meme.ts`; retire the `vesselIdentity.verifyingKey` fallback on every face
   relation. Red: the thief signs no dial, edge, enrolment, sibling, daemon ask, group open or meme. Control: A succeeds
   for A on each gate; B and no face refuse.
3. The relay S row (`carriage-relay.ts`, the relay port callers) and cadence (`carriage-caps.ts`, `node-caps.ts`). Red: the
   thief yields no relay key. Control: the row survives restart and proves only the relay.
4. The floor edges: seed-fed floor children, the flow pointer and the carrier pin route through the scoped place signer;
   the faceless carriage presents the public card. W14–W16 owns those files: if it has landed when you reach this slice,
   build them here; if it still runs, hand the controller patches.
5. The transitive census and the burn of every K15 exception.
Every red runs on node AND browser where the capability exists.

## Ground and fences
- Provision your own worktree per disk law (df first; stop under 60G on C:): `node tools/provision-worktree.mjs
  /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-bonds/wt`, then branch `feature/green-jello-dinosaur-5--k15-bonds` off the span head the
  controller names at launch. Build there only.
- Shared files: `open-node-vessel.ts` and `open-browser-vessel.ts` carry hunks of other lanes (D2's port hunks, W14–W16's
  card filing). Edit only the seed and identity hunks; merge the span into your lane before each push, and resolve any
  conflict by keeping both lanes' intent.
- Leave alone: D2's tw5 port and island files, `hand-gate.ts`, `tw5-projection.ts`, web `projection-sink.ts`; the W14–W16
  files while that lane runs (see slice 4); `vessel-kel.ts`'s grammar (consume it).
- Write the lane kit `bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-bonds-lane.mem` (reading as what stands), normalized twice;
  update `k15-custody-step-zero.mem`'s rows that change. The controller writes the road at the land.
- Crew, battery, commits, fences and hand-back exactly as the K17-R brief at `/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k17-r/brief.md`
  (sections Crew, Battery and landing, Fences, Hand-back), seat dirs under `/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-bonds/seats/`,
  resume sheet `/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/k15-bonds/resume.md`. The browser suite needs real Playwright browsers. Commit
  with plain commands only (`git commit -F <msg> --only -- <paths>`, one per commit; no shell functions, loops or
  heredocs). Build the end state: no "owed" item inside this mandate survives to the hand-back.
