+<<~ set hud="aim" mode="draft" mu="_!" stance="🏛️🗡️" aperture="16/arc" ooda-ha="✶ observe -> ⏿ orient -> ◇ decide -> ▶ act -> ↺ aftermath" drift-ward="I favor a compact ordered model; row prose may lag the head">>
+
+# Luna-Handwright: Lares (Tasked Spirit)
+
+Lares (Council), Lares (Ink-Clerk), Lares (Map-Wisp), Lares (Artificer), Lares (Advocate), Lares (Diplomat), Lares (Breach-Watch), Lares (Liminal): I stand the hands room as a fellow Lares. MEASURED means source at span head; LEAD means my synthesis. I2 below places the supplied scout result; I do not re-scout it.
+
+## ✶ Observe — what stands
+
+**Canon substrate.** The road says “A SESSION wears the face; the vessel wears none” and defines simultaneous sessions, face-scoped keys, and isolated planes (`stable-founding-road.mem:106-107`). The session contract is named as the hands authority (`.../api/pono/session-contract.mem`, #/the-hands and #/the-holder-protocol); the face intent plane landed PR #99. Road rows summarize status; the following are their measured status, not inferred completion:
+
+| Rows | MEASURED standing and gap |
+|---|---|
+| F1, F2 | Road `:592-593`: `session-document-view.ts`, `mountSurface`, `surface-recipe.ts` specified/built, but no production surface mounts through them; plugins still use `resolveRecipePluginCids`. Node and browser compose/mount callers, broad-sync replacement, per-session surface event gate and catalog asks remain. |
+| F3, F4, F5 | Road `:462-464`: one (face,wiki,slot) working doc; move node callers to sessions; bind receipts to face and make outcomes/effect index follow the working-layer reader; F5 node durability receipt. These remain owed rows; code has shared working layer and durable UDS receipt foundation (`packages/lararium-node/src/uds-channel.ts:116-168,275,639-646`), not proof of the whole session-scoped end state. |
+| F6, F9 | Road `:594,596`: browser holder routing/unicast and owner epoch/session/generation built; Repo and daemon moved to holder in part, slice four owed. Old vessel selector stores retired with K15 Wave D; additive switch act remains. |
+| F10, F11, F12 | Road `:465-467`: device fleet view/removal; watcher as leasing session, standing grant, Mask record field, person-edit versus agent-draft; draft writer attribution by session face. F12 specifically measures `modifier`/Automerge actor only, neither face-bound. |
+| P13, A8, B2, W17 | Road `:486,569,586,601`: per-meme grants/effective recipe; `persona wear` waits on session switch; two tabs/two faces/one holder; same-device switching and second joined face. Row text marks scope but gives no shipped claim. |
+| G13 | Road `:471`: summons lack writer check, tombstone every layer, in-memory dedup; owed writer check, working-only tombstone, durable dedup, lease/fence and `aud`. |
+| I2 | Scout handback `/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/i2-relay/sol/out.md:7-22`: no I2 road row; current I1 face plane has no delegation/revocation or intent relay, carriage relay is a different ciphertext transport. Place it after I1 (#99), before bake; model and red checks described by scout, not recertified here. |
+
+**Node/browser reality.** `open-node-vessel.ts` and `open-browser-vessel.ts` each compose broad vessel services and session-facing surfaces; the node still exposes a `carriageIdentity(..., p.wornFace() ? "face" : "place")` branch (`open-node-vessel.ts:3305-3309,3333-3334`), and one active-surface selector (`:2954-2957`). Browser options describe face presentation on open (`open-browser-vessel.ts:222-246`), and it hosts shared-holder routing. These are mixed vessel/session seams, not evidence every action already receives an explicit session capability. I2 scout measured I1 intent entry/reader/door and local-socket command, with no agent delegation (`sol/out.md:7,17`).
+
+## ⏿ Orient — model and joints
+
+**One end-state model (LEAD): “session is the hand.”** A session carries one selected face, capabilities, view, effective recipe, authored acts, draft authorship, and receipts. Vessel services serve sessions but do not supply a default identity. Face operation selects its atom explicitly; faceless operation stays faceless. This follows the road’s quoted session ruling, plus house laws “capability read by capability, never host” and “one name, one relation.” It joins F1–F6, F9–F12, A8, B2, W17, P13 and G13 where they alter the session’s view/action/effect boundary. Browser and node must share the model but can land platform slices separately.
+
+**Joints left open:**
+
+- **Session contract shape:** canon rules one face/session; house law derives explicit immutable session identity and per-session capability/view. Operator owns which fields persist in a session receipt; lean request/session id, face atom, capability proof, causal position, no wall-clock authority.
+- **Switch semantics:** canon says switch act additive and no selector persists (`road:596`); house law derives switch creates/replaces a session or changes that session’s face only after reauthorization. Operator owns in-place switch versus close/open UX; lean visible close-and-open transition so outstanding work cannot silently change face.
+- **Device removal view:** canon requires a person’s fleet view/removal (`road:466`) and no-global-now ruling. House law derives causal removal plus incomplete-history warning; operator owns “long silent” threshold (`#/decisions`), lean no clock expiry: show last causal contact, offer explicit removal.
+- **Receipts/drafts:** canon requires face-bound receipt and face as draft writer (`road:463,465`); house law derives signed/verified provenance and reader-visible distinction between verified face and user-entered `modifier`. Operator owns presentation fields; lean show author face, action, outcome, and pending/unknown state.
+- **G13 summons:** house row names writer check, working-only tombstone, durable dedup, lease/fence, `aud`; no operator fork apparent.
+
+Standalone: F10’s fleet UX/removal can ship after session identity exists; G13 can stand as a durable dispatch protocol if its writer capability is session-shaped. I2 stands alone as a relay protocol, but its agent identity must enter through session/face capability and K15’s key boundary. F5 durability receipt may stand alone only if it already binds the eventual face/session shape; otherwise fuse with F4.
+
+## ◇ Decide — order versus K15
+
+K15 should land before hands session integration, not fuse and not run parallel on shared identity files. Its brief says every face operation signs/opens by explicitly selected face atom under FCK, and faceless vessel needs no Keyhive identity. Session work consumes that contract; implementing early session receipts/callers against vessel identity would be re-cut. Measured overlap: K15 owns identity hunks in `open-node-vessel.ts` and `open-browser-vessel.ts`; hands owns the same composition files for session callers, with F6 slice 3 already co-landed with K15 step 3 (road `:594`). D2 owns neighboring TW5 port/island and `hand-gate.ts`; K15 explicitly fences those. Coordinate hunks, don’t edit across lane ownership. I2 uses separate relay admission key; it must not reuse K15 carriage relay-only S row as face authority (I2 scout `sol/out.md:22`).
+
+## ▶ Act — lanes in build order
+
+1. **Session switch and contract (before dependent hands lanes; after K15).** Rows F9, A8, W17; files `session-contract.ts`, persona command/store callers, `open-node-vessel.ts`, `open-browser-vessel.ts`, browser panel/session open, and targeted session tests. Red: two sessions choose different faces concurrently, switch never changes sibling session; control same-face re-open; positive node CLI and browser tab switch with explicit face and no persisted vessel selector. F9 selector retirement already built. D2 overlap: vessel composition only. K15 overlap: shared opens, K15 first.
+2. **Session view and hands runtime.** F1–F4, F6 remainder, F11; mesh view/recipe, node/browser mount and event routing, TW5 session dispatch, holder remainder, `verb-vm.ts`, `uds-channel.ts`. Red-first: no unscoped sync/catalog read, wrong face cannot invoke/edit, agent dissent cannot overwrite person edit, effect and receipt resolve under originating session after another face acts. Control existing same-session positive; known positive cross-platform scoped read and verb. D2 overlap: TW5 gate/projection files are D2; coordinate only interfaces. K15 overlap: open-vessel callers, after K15 identity cut.
+3. **Authored records and durability.** F5, F12, P13; `parallel-drafts.ts`, effect/outcome index and receipt paths, recipe resolver at actual mounts, reader UI. Red: forged `modifier` never proves authorship; receipt from other face not visible as own; wrong recipe/grant denied. Control unsigned display label remains explicitly unverified; positive session-signed change and readable durable result. D2 overlap low except TW5 draft surface; K15 selected-face signer dependency.
+4. **Person’s device and dispatch view.** F10, B2, G13; device list/removal and per-tab UI, summons/dispatcher, browser holder end slice. Red: two tabs show distinct face books; removed device loses access after causal fence; a summons cannot tombstone canon/other face and retry does not duplicate. Control retained device and unrelated face; positive explicit removal and durable receipt. D2 overlap projection/UI seam; K15 face edge/removal identity must precede. Land device genesis/identity changes before X0 bake.
+5. **I2 relay lane (parallel only after interface freeze).** Place supplied I2 design here, after I1 and K15 relay-key split. It owns intent-entry/read, delegation/revoke, relay admission and independent reader proof. Reds/controls/positive and D2/K15 boundaries: `/home/joshu/.lares-scratch/research/i2-relay/sol/out.md:17-22`. Identity/delegation genesis bytes precede bake.
+
+All lanes red-first (hostile case), then control (nearby valid refusal/behavior), then known positive. F10/F4/F5 and G13 alter identity, genesis or durable record shape: before founding bake. No CRDT document survives to the bake; rebuild from genesis, not migrate old mixed records.
+
+## Reader/person witness — LEAD
+
+Show two browser tabs over one vessel: tab A and tab B wear different faces and see only their own private books; switching A leaves B’s open work and identity unchanged. Show each face’s device roster, causal removal and the incomplete-history case; make a verb, close its caller, and let the person read a receipt naming face, action, result and any pending gap. In parallel drafts, identify the writer from the session proof, never `modifier`. Exercise agent dissent as a draft and a person’s direct edit as the person’s bounded act. Run these reds on node and browser where supported: no-face face operation; wrong-face view/write; cross-tab face bleed; stale session after switch; forged draft writer; receipt under wrong face; device removal before/after replica learns the event; summons targeting canon or another layer; replay after restart; hostile I2 relay changes args or uses revoked delegation. D2’s live projection must also prove the rendered control event returns only to its owning session.
+
+Stale text to repair at landing: F1/F2 describe modules as “specified”/no production caller despite the later road describing partial mounting pieces; F6 slice 3 is no longer owed; F9 says “switch act itself lands additive,” so should not imply selector persistence; F12’s writer description remains explicitly unbound; I2 is research-only absent road row. Measure each against the landing head before rewriting the road.
+
